@candidates

Purpose:
  Registry of knowledge candidates — the CANDIDATE tier of the
  knowledge lifecycle. Candidates are repeated observations that appear
  reusable but have not yet been validated by tests, tasks, or human
  review. This file is the canonical template for candidate entries and
  the promotion gate into validated references.

Use this index to evaluate whether a candidate is ready for promotion.

Owns: ./

Lifecycle Context:
  OBSERVED (insights/)
    ↓  3+ occurrences or strategic relevance
  CANDIDATE (this registry)
    ↓  evidence + human approval
  VALIDATED (references/)
    ↓  multi-project success
  ESTABLISHED (references/)

Entry Schema:
  Each candidate entry MUST carry the following fields:

  Fields:
    id:               @candidate.<name>
    canonical_name:    human-readable preferred term
    definition:        single-sentence description
    aliases:           [alternative names that mean the same]
    related:           [related candidates or references]
    purpose:           one-line statement of the practice
    origin:            @insight.<name> that originated this candidate
    observed_in:       [contexts where observed]
    evidence_count:    integer (total evidence sources gathered)
    by_type:
      code:          integer
      tests:         integer
      tasks:         integer
      decisions:     integer
      projects:      integer
      production:    integer
      external:      integer
      human:         integer
    trust:            low (default — no validation yet)
    confidence:       low | medium
    status:           candidate
    conflicts_with:    [references this may conflict with]
    promotion_target: optional @reference.* target on promotion
    promoted_to:      @reference.* / @skill.* / @pattern.* (on success)
    expired_at:        YYYY-MM-DD (auto-set 30 days after creation;
                        candidates not promoted by this date expire)

  Example:
    @candidate.idempotent-command
      canonical_name: Idempotent Command
      definition: A command that produces the same result regardless of
                  how many times it is executed.
      aliases:
        - duplicate protection
        - retry-safe operation
      related:
        - @candidate.exactly-once
      purpose: Prevent duplicate command execution.
      origin: @insight.retry-pattern
      observed_in:
        - tmp/payment-service
        - tmp/order-service
      evidence_count: 2
      by_type:
        code: 2
        tests: 0
        tasks: 0
        projects: 2
      trust: low
      confidence: low
      status: candidate
      conflicts_with: []
      expired_at: 2026-09-30

Promotion Gate:
  A candidate MAY be promoted to VALIDATED when ALL of the following hold:
    [C1] evidence_count >= 2 independent sources with at least one
         test or human review.
    [C2] No unresolved conflicts-with an established reference.
    [C3] Human reviewer approves via the promotion workflow.
    [C4] The candidate has been canonicalized per CANONICALIZATION.sdd.

  On promotion:
    - A new @skill.* / @pattern.* / @architecture.* entry is created
      in .sdd/references/.
    - status becomes validated.
    - trust becomes medium / confidence medium.
    - This @candidate.* entry is marked deprecated with a
      promoted_to pointer.

Expiration Policy:
  [C5] Candidates expire 30 days after creation without promotion.
  [C6] Expired candidates are moved to .sdd/knowledge/lessons/
       with reason.expired_unpromoted.
  [C7] Expired candidates are NEVER deleted — archived for history.

Rules:
  [R1] AI MUST NOT auto-promote a candidate without evidence and
       human approval.
  [R2] Each candidate MUST link back to its originating @insight.*.
  [R3] Conflicting candidates MUST be flagged, not guessed.
  [R4] Duplicate candidates MUST propose a merge per
       CANONICALIZATION.sdd merge protocol.
  [R5] Candidates with trust.low and 0 evidence are reviewed
       within 7 days or archived.

